<title>USA: Einstein/Noah says suit 'groundless'.</title>
<headline>Einstein/Noah says suit 'groundless'.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Einstein/Noah Bagel Corp said Monday that a class action lawsuit filed against it was &quot;groundless&quot; and that it would defend itself &quot;vigorously.&quot;</p>
<p>The Seattle law firm of Cohen, Milstein, Hausfeld &amp; Toll said the stockholder suit alleges that Einstein and some of its officers and directors violated federal securities laws.</p>
<p>A statement issued by the law firm did not indicate the court in which the lawsuit was filed. The attorneys could not be reached for comment.</p>
</text>
